                                "sense_id": "e4551f3d-f65d-3019-bf2b-b45e2101bde7",
                                "text": "The ear-shaped or branchiform stigma of Otostigma and Branchiostoma is due to the oblique form of the cone along a small part of its length; on the base of the stigmata of these forms there appear a few of those irregular darkly coloured patches, beset with small hooks, which are so common in the Chilopoda."
